%S A398640 0,0,0,1,20,3749,1877695,1505997049
%N A398640 Number of quasi-quintic graphs on 2*n + 1 vertices.
%C A398640 A quasi-quintic graph is a simple graph with one vertex of degree 6 and all other vertices of degree 5. By the handshake lemma, such a graph necessarily has odd order.
%H A398640 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Quasi-QuinticGraph.html">Quasi-Quintic Graph</a>.
%e A398640 a(7) = 1505997049 because there are 1505997049 quasi-quintic graphs on 15 vertices.
%Y A398640 Cf. A398638 (quasi-cubic graphs).
%Y A398640 Cf. A398639 (connected quasi-cubic graphs).
%Y A398640 Cf. A398641 (connected quasi-quintic graphs).
